{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.RigidDualizingComplex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.RigidDualizingComplex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Homology.HomologicalComplex","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Defs"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.rigidDualizingComplex_inhabited_trivially","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.rigidDualizingComplex_inhabited_trivially","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L61-L96","doc":"**The structure is inhabited — and this is NOT Yekutieli's existence\ntheorem.**  Renamed and re-stated 2026-09-07; read the scope before\nciting it.\n\nIt used to be called `rigid_dualizing_exists`, docstringed as \"Existence\nof a rigid dualizing complex for a suitable non-commutative algebra\nsatisfying van den Bergh conditions\", and proved by setting all three\n`Prop` fields to `True`.  Two things were wrong with that.  The\nhypotheses it names — \"suitable\", \"van den Bergh conditions\" — appear\nnowhere in the statement, which quantifies over EVERY ring; and\nYekutieli's Theorem 4.2 does not hold for every ring.  So the name and\ndocstring claimed a theorem the statement does not make.\n\nWith the fields encoded, the witness has to satisfy them, and it still\ncan: `carrier = rhomEnv = A`, the identity equivalence, `injDim =\nhomdim = 0`, `vdbDual = id`.  **That is the point of keeping it.**\nEncoding the fields narrowed what a witness must supply — an `Equiv`, a\nnumeric bound, an involution — without making the trivial model\nimpossible, and a theorem that exhibits the trivial model is the honest\nrecord of how much was bought.\n\nWhat it establishes: the axioms are consistent.  What it does not: that\nany *interesting* rigid dualizing complex exists, which needs the\nderived-category infrastructure Mathlib lacks.  See [yekutieli2015]\nTheorem 4.2 for the real construction and its real hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.vdb_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.vdb_duality","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L58-L58","doc":"**Van den Bergh duality**: the duality is an involution.  Was a `Prop`\nfield naming the property without stating it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.vdbDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.vdbDual","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The van den Bergh duality functor on the carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.finite_inj_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.finite_inj_dim","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L53-L53","doc":"**Finite injective dimension**, bounded by the homological dimension.\nWas a `Prop` field; \"finite\" is now a stated bound between two\nnumbers the structure already carries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.injDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.injDim","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Injective dimension of the complex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.rigidifying_iso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.rigidifying_iso","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L47-L47","doc":"**The rigidifying isomorphism** `ω_A• ≃ RHom_{A^e}(A, A^e)`.\n\nWas `rigidifying_iso : Prop`, a field typed with the *universe* `Prop`,\nso the instance chose the proposition and `True` discharged it. An\nisomorphism is DATA; it is now an `Equiv`, which is the weakest form\nthat still says the two objects correspond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.rhomEnv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.rhomEnv","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L40-L40","doc":"`RHom_{A^e}(A, A^e)`, the object the rigidifying isomorphism lands in.\nCarried as a field because the derived-category construction is not in\nMathlib — which is what made the old `Prop` field look forced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.homdim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.homdim","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Homological dimension of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.carrier","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The carrier type for the dualizing complex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RigidDualizingComplex","kind":"structure","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.lean#L21-L58","doc":"**RigidDualizingComplex**: a rigid dualizing complex `ω_A•` for\na non-commutative algebra `A`, in the sense of Yekutieli.\n\nThe complex is equipped with a rigidifying isomorphism\n`ω_A• ≃ RHom_{A^e}(A, A^e)`, ensuring uniqueness up to\nunique isomorphism.\n\nUniverse-carrying structure (§7d U2): the carrier universe `v` is\npinned so use sites can tie it explicitly.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:rigid-dualizing-complex}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:rigid-dualizing-complex","label":"def:rigid-dualizing-complex","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/rigid-dualizing-complex.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}